Now, for example, in Latin America, we do have this, what we call sometimes the Latino time or Hispanic time, which is like nine o'clock is like the time that everyone should be there.

190
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:33,560
But until people get there, get their coffee and whatever, then it'll be 9.15, maybe up to 9.30.

191
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:39,880
